+++ b/NOTES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@
+# Demand forecasting module
+
+Nothing could be run in this environment (no PHP, no database), so none of this has been executed. It was written
+against the code and SQL in the repository and checked by reading only.
+
+## What was built
+
+A **Forecasting** main-menu module (`modulelink` `forecast`, report link `fcst`) placed right after Manufacturing.
+
+### Pages (all new, in the repository root)
+
+| Page | What it does | Page security token |
+|---|---|---|
+| `ForecastSalesHistory.php` | Extract sales history for a month range, show range / months / items held | 11 |
+| `ForecastGenerate.php` | Generate forecasts for one item or a whole category, 12 methods or best fit, result list with reasons | 11 |
+| `ForecastReview.php` | Search active forecasts, period by period calculated / revised / last year / variance, enter revised quantities | 11 |
+| `ForecastSummary.php` | Summary forecasts by category, customer type, sales area, salesperson, plus review of the detail behind one | 11 |
+| `ForecastToMRP.php` | Convert active forecasts to MRP demands (replace / incremental) | 11 |
+| `ForecastDashboard.php` | Counts, history range, links | 2 |
+| `ForecastInquiry.php` | Forecasts by item, category, location, period | 2 |
+| `ForecastAccuracy.php` | MAD, POA, MSE, RMSE per item, category and method, low-accuracy flag | 2 |
+| `ForecastMethodComparison.php` | One item, several methods side by side on a hold-out, with accuracy | 2 |
+| `ForecastParameters.php` | Company-wide defaults (alpha, beta, gamma, season length, MA periods, hold-out months, horizon) | 15 |
+
+Tokens: 2 = basic reports/inquiries, 11 = inventory management, 15 = administration. I used 11 rather than 9 (which the
+MRP pages use) because the installer data gives token 9 to the supplier log-on role.
+The Forecasting menu also links the existing `MRPDemands.php` (master schedule), `MRP.php` (run) and `MRPReport.php`.
+
+`includes/ForecastFunctions.php` holds everything else: history extraction, the methods, best fit, accuracy measures,
+saving forecasts, MRP conversion.
+
+### Tables
+
+`forecastsaleshistory` (item, location, customer type, area, salesperson, month, net quantity),
+`forecasthistorymonths` (one row per extracted month, so the history end is known even for a month without sales),
+`forecasts` + `forecastdetails` (calculated and revised quantity per period),
+`forecastsummaries` + `forecastsummarydetails`, `forecastmrplinks` (which `mrpdemands` rows the module wrote).
+Settings are `config` rows `ForecastAlpha`, `ForecastBeta`, `ForecastGamma`, `ForecastSeasonLength`,
+`ForecastMAPeriods`, `ForecastHoldoutMonths`, `ForecastHorizon`. MRP demand type `FCST` ("Demand Forecast").
+
+### Delivery
+
+* **Existing databases:** `sql/updates/44.php` (tables, config, demand type, module, scripts, menu items,
+  user module lists). The runner picks it up through `HighestFileName`.
+* **New installations:** `install/sql/tables/forecast*.sql`, and the matching rows in `install/sql/data/{modules,
+  menuitems,scripts,config}.sql` and the new `install/sql/data/mrpdemandtypes.sql`; the demo installer
+  (`install/sql/demo.sql`) gets the same rows. The installer sets `DBUpdateNumber` to the highest update file, so
+  update 44 does not run on a fresh install; the seed data therefore has to carry everything.
+* **User access:** `WWW_Users.php` has the new module line. `CustLoginSetup.php` / `SuppLoginSetup.php` module strings
+  got the extra entry.
+* **Translations:** all text uses `__()`; the update script wraps module and menu captions in `__()` like the other
+  update scripts, so the next `.pot` rebuild picks them up. I did not regenerate `.pot`/`.po` files.
+
+## Where the sales history comes from, and how it reaches MRP
+
+History comes from `stockmoves` of type 10 (sales invoice) and 11 (credit note) with `hidemovt=0`, quantity negated,
+the same selection `InventoryPlanning.php` and `SalesInquiry.php` use. So invoiced quantities with credits deducted,
+never open orders. It is grouped by calendar month of `trandate`, location, and the customer's type, the branch's area
+and salesperson (this is what lets summaries be built from the same history). Re-extracting a range deletes that range
+(and its month rows) first, in one transaction.
+
+MRP: `ForecastToMRP.php` writes one `mrpdemands` row per item and month (due on the first of the month) under demand
+type `FCST`, quantity = revised quantity if present, else calculated. The existing MRP run reads `mrpdemands` when
+"use master schedule demands" is chosen, so nothing in `MRP.php` changed. Every row written is recorded in
+`forecastmrplinks` (FK to `mrpdemands`, `ON DELETE CASCADE`). Replace mode deletes only linked rows of the same items
+inside the horizon before inserting; incremental mode skips months that already have a linked row. Both are idempotent.
+Hand-entered demands, or demands from other sources, are never in the link table, so they are never touched, even if a
+user had already created a demand type called `FCST`.
+
+## Things worth knowing / decisions on ambiguous points
+
+* **Module position vs. user access (the risky part).** `www_users.modulesallowed` is a positional list: entry n is the
+  n-th module by `modules.sequence`. Inserting Forecasting at sequence 7 shifts General Ledger, Asset Manager, Petty Cash,
+  Setup and Utilities, which would have silently changed every existing user's access. Update 44 therefore inserts a `0`
+  at that position in every user's list first (padding/truncating to the role's module count), and only then adds the
+  module. Existing users keep exactly their modules and do not get Forecasting until an administrator sets it. The
+  rewrite only runs while the module does not exist, in a transaction. The column was widened from 25 to 50 (also in
+  `install/sql/tables/www_users.sql`) because a 12-module list is 24 characters. Users must log in again to see changes.
+* **Active forecast** is enforced by the database: `forecasts.activeslot` is 1 for the active one and NULL otherwise,
+  with a unique key on (item, location, activeslot). Regenerating clears the old slot and inserts the new row in one
+  transaction; the superseded forecast stays with its method, parameters and revisions (accuracy uses them).
+  Same for summaries.
+* **All locations vs a location.** Location `''` means all locations combined. An item can have both. For MRP, which has
+  no location, an all-locations forecast wins; otherwise the location forecasts are summed. Never both, so no double count.
+* **History length.** An item's series starts at its first month with sales (earlier months are not its history) and
+  runs to the last month held. Months with net negative sales count as zero demand. If extracted months have gaps, only
+  the unbroken run ending at the last month is used, with a warning on the history page. Forecasts start the month after
+  the last month held. Series are clamped, and all forecasts are rounded to 2 decimals and never negative; revised
+  quantities must be >= 0.
+* **Method definitions the BRD leaves open.** 5 Linear approximation: line through the latest month and the month
+  "periods between points" earlier (default 5, so 6 months needed). 8 Flexible: weights for the previous 12 months,
+  not normalised, defaulting to equal weights. 9 Weighted MA: weights normalised, latest first, default 40/30/20/10.
+  2 Calculated percent: last 12 months / prior 12 months, fails with a reason when the prior year had no sales.
+  1/2/3 beyond 12 periods compound on the already forecast month. 12 Holt-Winters is additive; its minimum is two seasons.
+  Alpha/beta/gamma are limited to 0.1-0.9 (the BRD gives that range for alpha only).
+* **Best fit.** Ranking is by MAD over the held-out months (RMSE breaks ties), using only methods the shorter history
+  allows. "Best fit for each item" picks per item; "Best fit across the category" scores each method by MAD relative to
+  the item's average held-out sales, averaged over the items it could be tested on, and only methods testable on at
+  least half the items compete. That one method is then applied to all items, and items it cannot forecast are listed
+  as failures.
+* **POA.** Defined as total forecast / total actual x 100 (100 = perfect). "Low accuracy" = POA more than 30 points from
+  100, or no actual sales. Variance highlight in review = 25% or more against last year. Both are constants in
+  `ForecastFunctions.php`, not settings.
+* **Accuracy basis.** Only forecast periods whose month is in the held history are compared; where several forecasts
+  (active and superseded) cover the same item, location and month, the latest counts. The quantity compared is the
+  revised one when present.
+* **Active item** for category runs: not discontinued and not a dummy (`mbflag D`) item.
+* **Batch generation** runs in one request and prints progress every 25 items, then the result list; there is no
+  background job (cron/email automation is out of scope).
+* **Not done:** no per-user location restriction (`locationusers`) is applied on the forecasting pages; no manual
+  chapter; the converted MRP demand does not follow later revisions until the conversion is run again.
+* **Existing repository drift I noticed and left alone:** the install table files still declare `stockid varchar(20)`
+  although update 43 widens it to 64; the new tables use 64 and have no foreign key on `stockid`, so they work either way.
+  `sql/demo.sql` (old copy, not used by the installer) was not touched.
